ma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=9$ and the sample size $n=30,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{9}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
